/*! \page Solver_paramFile Solver parameter file

The solver reads all its input from one text file. The Python bridge writes the file with \ref py_utils::cpp_bridge::write_param_file "write_param_file()" and starts the solver as:

\verbatim
solver --param_file=<path>
\endverbatim

The executable is named solver.exe on Windows. The function build_parameters() in radcluster_code/cpp_utils/core/parameters.h reads the file into the struct Parameters. After that, the right-hand side performs only arithmetic.

\section Solver_paramFile_format Format

The file has one entry per line, of the form:

\verbatim
key=value
\endverbatim

An array is written as indexed entries:

\verbatim
KVV_0=<value>
KVV_1=<value>
...
\endverbatim

\section Solver_paramFile_keys Groups of keys

| Group | Examples |
|---|---|
| cluster size limits | I, V |
| solver mode and physics option | window_mode, physics_option_int, he_mode |
| geometric prefactors | A_sph, A_loop, B_rot, L_hat |
| mobility cut-offs | i_mobile, v_mobile |
| vacancy rate arrays | KVV_k, KVI_k, GVV_k, KHeV_k, Pr_VAC_k |
| SIA rate arrays | KII_k, KIV_k, GII_k, k2_SIA_k, Pr_SIA_k, K_1D_pref_k |
| loop conversion | loop_conversion, n_loop_min, Gamma_uni_k, K_100_grow_k |
| bin moments | I_bin, V_bin, i_discrete, v_discrete, r_ratio, shape_function |
| initial condition | y0_k |
| integration | t_begin, t_end, n_points, log_time, rtol, atol, hmin, hmax, max_order |
| linear solver | linsol, mu, ml, prec_type, prec_bw, prec_rank |
| sliding window | window_width, window_pad, window_pad_v, window_check_every |

In window_mode the value 0 is full_system and the value 4 is active_window. In physics_option_int the values 0 to 3 are full_CD_fission, full_CD_fusion, bin_moment_CD_fission and bin_moment_CD_fusion.

The key sia_emission_monomer selects whether the monomer of an SIA thermal emission is returned to the monomer pool (1) or dropped (0). The value 0 reproduces results obtained before version 2.1.2.

\section Solver_paramFile_output Output

The solver writes n_points rows of (1 + N_eq) values as raw float64 numbers to a companion file with the extension .bin. Each row holds the time and the state vector (see \ref Core_stateLayout). The file is flushed after every row, so that a partial output survives an interrupt.

\b Note that the parameter file is an internal interface between the Python layer and the solver. Physics parameters belong in the input workbook. See \ref IO_input.

\sa \ref IO_output

*/
